architect-cell-ref-ruling-of-record.md:21:7. **The entry-key (`:yang.call/entry`) admission policy is OUT OF SCOPE** — it stays exactly as landed and gated in D2 (an unadmitted entry-shaped map refuses; pinned clojure_test.clj:2600). \"Ordinary map application always remains data\" is therefore true for the cell-ref language, not universally; §8.10 documents the entry-key policy as the one declared shape-routed exception.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794330000000-architect-cell-ref-ruling-of-record.md:25:§8.10 (yang.antlr.md) gains: the `cell/authentic?` vocabulary entry; the position/semantics rule (routing consults the heap for cell-ref-shaped callees); the bearer-copy semantic (rule 4); the bag semantic clarification (a reference stored in data REMAINS a reference — storage changes nothing; what decides is the authentication query at the call); and the entry-key exception note (rule 7). The cell-profiles publication and any module docs listing the vocabulary update accordingly.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:41:master since: captured continuations are invocable on all four VMs\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:209:  staging and outcome handling.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:386:compiler outcome. None causes automatic dependency downloading or\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:506:|               | grammar without a Dart helper | outcome                  |\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:592:character stream is not a portable asynchronous continuation protocol.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:606:boundaries. A native ANTLR call stack is not a Yin continuation and is\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:668:one-pass recursive preorder walk and outcome-specific contracts\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:672:own outcome), and a portable `conform` is the per-target oracle. A\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:783:Backpressure is the stream's own `full` and `blocked` outcomes, handled\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:871:compiler coordinator consumes those descriptors and appends outcomes.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:874:### 6.2 Respec