ts body under the\\n     9\\t   donor runtime's own entry (`js/run-main`, `php/run-main`, `py/run-main`,\\n    10\\t   `clj/run-main`), reads each named export from the donor runtime's global\\n    11\\t   namespace, and projects it into the caller runtime's namespace under the\\n    12\\t   same name; then the caller source, lowered unmodified, runs under its own\\n    13\\t   entry. The composition is a sequence of top-level nodes: no call node is\\n    14\\t   rewritten, no foreign `:code` is extracted, no language-pair wrapper is\\n    15\\t   inserted, and the projected value is the donor's own callable value\\n    16\\t   (identity survives).\\n    17\\t\\n    18\\t   A callable value is task-local (a function is a cell, and cells are\\n    19\\t   task-local, section 8.11), so the export is answered as a node evaluated\\n    20\\t   in the caller's task, never as a host value carried between tasks.\\n    21\\t   `export-program` answers the donor's export alone as the program's value.\\n    22\\t\\n    23\\t   Every program runs linked on the three vector VMs (`semantic`, `stack`,\\n    24\\t   `register`) over the TypeScript linked harness's content store, where\\n    25\\t   `yang.call` and `js` already live and `php`, `py` and `clj` are\\n    26\\t   published beside them. The AST walker is not a backend: its links are\\n    27\\t   refused until L-b.\\\"\\n    28\\t  (:require\\n    29\\t    [clojure.string :as str]\\n    30\\t    [yang.clojure :as clj-comp]\\n    31\\t    [yang.clojure.prelude :as clj-prelude]\\n    32\\t    [yang.core.module :as core-module]\\n    33\\t    [yang.core.names :as names]\\n    34\\t    [yang.core.uast :as u]\\n    35\\t    [yang.php.antlr.cst :as php-cst]\\n    36\\t    [yang.php.antlr.lower :as php-lower]\\n    37\\t    [yang.php.antlr.portable-harness :as php-h]\\n    38\\t    [yang.php.antlr.prelude :as php-prelude]\\n    39\\t    [yang.python.antlr.lower :as py-lower]\\n    40\\t    [yang.python.antlr.parser :as py-pars