**Ruling: (B).** The entry-absent library value path produces a `:yang.call/thrown` condition whose value is the `:yang.call/not-callable` map:

```clojure
{:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown
 :yang.call/value
 {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/not-callable
  :yang.call/data {:yang.call/callee f}}}
```

At site #7, `invoke-value` executes a source-level `throw` of a condition-shaped map. That map is not an authenticated retained condition, so [§8.10.7](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-r3-orch/docs/design/yang.antlr.md:3838) requires the boundary to treat it as the payload of a new thrown condition. The green protocol rows are consistent with this: their refusals travel through `yang.call/transfer` to a real raise exit as protocol conditions. The value path has no such transfer.

This does not violate R5: the compiler’s boundary constructs the outer condition; no source-writable key authenticates the inner map. Nor does it break R3: this is first construction from a thrown value, not forwarding an unchanged retained protocol condition. R3 continues to require an already-retained protocol condition to be forwarded intact. The token remains exclusively a provenance mechanism for that distinction.

**Minimal fix instruction:**

- Keep the site #7 `:else` in [clojure.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-r3-orch/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2799) as a throw of the unmarked `yang.call/condition` map. Correct the adjacent comment: the boundary wraps that thrown value and authenticates the **new outer condition**; the library does not cause the inner map to be stamped. Do not use `(f)`, which re-enters the dispatcher.
- In [clojure_test.clj](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-r3-orch/test/yang/clojure_test.clj:2599), update the five affected assertions at lines 2599, 2619, 2635, 2736, and 2766 in both lanes to expect the outer `:yang.call/thrown` and inspect the inner `:yang.call/not-callable` and its callee evidence. Preserve the error-tag, termination, and budget assertions. The entry-present admission assertions remain raw protocol refusals.
- Retain the already-directed token equality, token stamping at sites #1–#6, and `remark-tails` changes. Run the affected tests and the protocol and shape conformance rows after the fix.

No implementation changes were made.
